## 3. The 10 Backend Engineering Commandments (Summary)

```mermaid
flowchart LR
  Req["Request"] --> RL["07. Rate Limiter"] --> Sec["13. Helmet / Security"] --> Val["03. Input Validation"] --> Auth["02. Auth & RBAC"]
  Auth --> Cache{"06. Cache?"}
  Cache -->|Hit| Fast["⚡ <5ms Response"]
  Cache -->|Miss| DB["05. Indexed PostgreSQL DB"]
  DB --> BG["08. Async Background Queue"]
  DB -.->|Error| Err["04. Global Error Handler"]
  DB --> Log["10. Structured Logger"]
```

| # | Principle | Production Implementation |
|---|---|---|
| **02** | **Auth & Authorization 🔐** | `bcryptjs` password hashing, HMAC-SHA256 JWTs, strict RBAC (`STUDENT`, `ALUMNI`, `FACULTY`, `ADMIN`). |
| **03** | **Validate Every Request ⚠️** | Strict schema validation on request body, query params, and file MIME types/sizes (resumes $\le$ 5MB). |
| **04** | **Centralized Error Handling 🚨** | Global Express error middleware returning uniform `{ success, data/message, code }` envelope. |
| **05** | **Database Design Matters 🗄️** | Prisma B-Tree indexes on `batchYear`, `department`, `company`; pagination (`limit=20`); and `Serializable` transactions. |
| **06** | **Don't Hit DB Every Time ⚡** | In-memory LRU cache (`node-cache`) for dashboard stats and directory filter lists. |
| **07** | **Add Rate Limiting 🚦** | 100 req/min global limit; 5 req/min on `/api/auth/login` to prevent brute-force attacks. |
| **08** | **Use Queues for Heavy Tasks ✉️** | Non-blocking async background workers for emails and uploads (<50ms API response time). |
| **09** | **Don't Deploy Untested Code 🧪** | Automated pre-deploy test suites verifying cloud storage, emails, RSVPs, and search queries. |
| **10** | **Structured Logging 📝** | Morgan/Pino JSON logger tracking response times, status codes, and slow queries (>500ms). |
| **13** | **Secure Your Production Env 🛡️** | Zero leaked credentials in git, Helmet.js headers, strict CORS, and XSS sanitization. |

